<title>USA: Visioneer Q1 shr loss $0.89 vs profit nil.</title>
<headline>Visioneer Q1 shr loss $0.89 vs profit nil.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>VISIONEER, INC.</p>
<p>				    STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								 March 31,</p>
<p> (in thousands, except per share amounts)	1997	1996</p>
<p> Net revenues					  $10,048  $18,206</p>
<p> Cost of revenues				     17,595   11,247</p>
<p> Gross profit / (loss)			     (7,547)    6,959</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>     Research and development			3,030    2,372</p>
<p>     Selling, general and administrative	 6,889    5,133</p>
<p>	   Total operating expenses		  9,919    7,505</p>
<p> Operating loss				     (17,466)    (546)</p>
<p> Other income						333	603</p>
<p>Income (loss) before provision for income taxes</p>
<p>							  (17,133)     (57)</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes			   0.00     0.00</p>
<p> Net income / (loss)			     ( 17,133)	 57</p>
<p> Net income / (loss) per share		   ( 0.89)  ( 0.00)</p>
<p>Average common and common equivalent</p>
<p>     shares outstanding			     19,282   20,462</p>
<p>Note - Latest Q1 loss includes charges of $9.5 million for write-downs related to realignment of manufacturing operations due to product transitions. In addition, the company took a charge of $2.5 million for price protection. Without these adjustments, the net loss for the quarter would have been $5.2 million or $0..27 a share.</p>
